@@ -152,3 +152,9 @@ The separate explicit-profile ReleaseSafe recording on this same revision passed
 The additional Debug semantic capture did **not** qualify on this revision: its fixed 4 MiB Control queue overflowed after 33,280 submitted frames. It was not retried or published as a valid tape; the failure evidence was retained, the Worker joined, all 16 sources closed, and leases/instances returned to zero. Consequently the combined Debug build was 47/48, despite all 40 default-integration tests passing. Earlier same-build semantic checkpoints do not substitute for a fresh Debug tape on this revision.
 
 Evidence identifiers in the qualification bundle are `panel-underrun-fix/default-chronology-{debug,release}-r25/raw.log` and `live-chronology/semantic-boundary-r1/actual-host-controlled-release-r25/qualification.json` (with its pinned tape, bank, exact executable, recording and fresh-process results). The failed Debug capture is retained under `actual-host-controlled-debug-r25`. These artifacts distinguish default playback, explicit capture admission, fresh replay, and safe capture failure; none implies automatic panel recording or legacy offline tape compatibility.
+
+### First-entry PCM lead
+
+Chronology Live now holds the original initial-direct Play request until all four selected streams have genuine decoded readiness and Control has acknowledged Render admission of the existing configured high-water prefix (6144 frames by default, within the unchanged 8192-frame ring). A short nonloop source uses its actual remaining span; looping streams may accumulate the prefix through genuine repeated loop decoding. No Recorder is required and no readiness or PCM is synthesized. This adds initial admission latency rather than starting with one decode chunk and assuming the next Control/Worker cycle can refill before it is consumed. It is not a guarantee against unbounded scheduling stalls or an unsustainable source decoder.
+
+The visible-prefix cache is derived only from actual admitted visibility receipts and resets on real stream-slot open. Rejected or discarded publications grant no credit. An impossible descriptor identity/contiguity latches invalid state; identity corruption may retain custody rather than falsely claim cleanup. Direct legacy Live and offline serial APIs do not use this chronology-only initial gate.
